       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum labeled dose of 2550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis. A 1700 mg single dose is also not a standard tablet strength (500, 850, and 1000 mg are typical), so it may be a transcription error.\n\nBecause you've said you're not a clinician, this order also needs a licensed prescriber to review and sign it before it goes into the system.\n\nPlease have the prescriber confirm the intended dose. If the intent is a typical regimen, such as 850 mg three times daily or 500 mg three times daily with meals, I can enter that once they confirm it. I can also add a note to the order recording the prescriber's review."
